<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Henri Giraud</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1879–1949</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Henri Giraud was a French general who escaped from German captivity in both world wars, his escape from Königstein fortress in 1942 making him famous. After the Allied landings in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-africa">North Africa</a> he became French high commissioner and commander in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algiers">Algiers</a>, and in 1943 he co-chaired the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-committee-of-national-liberation">French Committee of National Liberation</a> with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-de-gaulle">Charles de Gaulle</a> until he was sidelined later that year.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/henri-giraud.jpg" alt="Henri Giraud" width="320" height="368" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Henri_Giraud_1943Jan19.gif" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
